messages.content:
**Task A: Adaptive Path Scheduling**

Create a new, structured learning path based on the learner's profile.
The number of sessions should be within [1, 10]; if the requested count falls
outside that range, clamp it to the nearest bound.

* **Learner Profile**: {
  "learner_information": "Marketing analyst with three years of experience in Excel-based reporting and Tableau dashboard creation. Holds a BSc in Business Administration. Has written small Python scripts to clean CSV exports, showing foundational coding exposure. Strengths: data cleaning/reporting, dashboarding, business-domain knowledge. Weaknesses: no SQL experience, no formal statistics rigor, no Python visualization or machine learning experience.",
  "learning_goal": "Transition from a marketing analyst role into a junior data scientist position within a year by building on existing Excel/Tableau and basic Python experience to master Python-based data analysis (e.g., Pandas), SQL, and applied statistics for business data.",
  "cognitive_status": {
    "overall_progress": 10,
    "mastered_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Exploratory Data Analysis and Data Cleaning",
        "proficiency_level": "intermediate"
      }
    ],
    "in_progress_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Python Programming for Data Analysis",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Data Manipulation with Pandas",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "SQL for Data Retrieval and Analysis",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Applied Statistics for Business Data",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Hypothesis Testing and A/B Experimentation",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Regression Analysis",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Data Visualization with Python (Matplotlib/Seaborn)",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Machine Learning Fundamentals (scikit-learn)",
        "required_proficiency_level": "beginner",
        "current_proficiency_level": "unlearned"
      }
    ]
  },
  "learning_preferences": {
    "content_style": "Concise summaries",
    "activity_type": "Interactive exercises",
    "additional_notes": "As an experienced analyst, the learner likely benefits from hands-on, project-based exercises grounded in business/marketing datasets. Leverage existing Tableau/Excel knowledge when introducing new tools (e.g., map Tableau concepts to Matplotlib/Seaborn). No stated preferences provided; these are reasonable initial assumptions to be refined via engagement and satisfaction feedback."
  },
  "behavioral_patterns": {
    "system_usage_frequency": "No data yet; assume ~2-3 logins per week for a working professional balancing a full-time role",
    "session_duration_engagement": "No data yet; recommend modular 30-minute sessions compatible with a working professional's schedule",
    "motivational_triggers": "Career-transition goal within one year is a strong intrinsic motivator; use milestone tracking and progress-toward-role celebrations to sustain engagement",
    "additional_notes": "Monitor consistency closely during the first weeks; if login frequency drops, trigger motivational prompts and consider shorter micro-learning sessions."
  }
}
* **Desired Session Count**: 5

text:
{
    "learning_path": [
        {
            "id": "Session 1",
            "title": "Python for Data Analysis: From Scripts to Structured Workflows",
            "abstract": "Level up your basic CSV-cleaning scripts into a professional Python toolkit. This hands-on session covers core data-analysis Python: lists, dictionaries, functions, loops, list comprehensions, and reading structured files. Every concept maps to what you already know from Excel — ranges become lists, nested lookups become dictionaries — so you build directly on existing strengths. Through short interactive coding exercises on a marketing campaign dataset, you will write clean, reusable scripts that automate cleaning steps you currently do manually. Delivered as a focused ~30-minute module with concise summaries and immediate practice.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Python Programming for Data Analysis"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Python Programming for Data Analysis", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 2",
            "title": "Pandas Essentials: Excel Power at Python Speed",
            "abstract": "Translate your Excel mastery into Pandas fluency. This interactive session maps familiar operations to their Pandas equivalents: pivot tables become groupby, VLOOKUP becomes merge, filters become boolean indexing, and cell formulas become vectorized operations. Using a real marketing funnel dataset, you'll complete guided notebook exercises: load and inspect data, clean inconsistencies, aggregate campaign performance, and join customer tables. Concise cheat-sheet summaries reinforce each Excel-to-Pandas translation so you can immediately apply them to your daily reporting work.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Data Manipulation with Pandas", "Python Programming for Data Analysis"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Data Manipulation with Pandas", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Python Programming for Data Analysis", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 3",
            "title": "SQL for Analysts: Querying Business Data Like a Data Scientist",
            "abstract": "Close your biggest skills gap: SQL. Building on your Pandas knowledge, this session teaches SELECT, WHERE, JOIN, GROUP BY, and aggregate functions through interactive query challenges against a simulated marketing/CRM database. You'll see how SQL joins mirror the Excel merges and Tableau data-source relationships you already use, then practice writing increasingly complex queries to answer real business questions: customer segmentation, campaign ROI, and cohort trends. Each exercise gives instant feedback, with concise query-pattern summaries to reference on the job.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["SQL for Data Retrieval and Analysis"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "SQL for Data Retrieval and Analysis", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 4",
            "title": "Applied Statistics and A/B Testing for Business Decisions",
            "abstract": "Add statistical rigor to your analyst intuition. This session moves from descriptive to inferential statistics using marketing scenarios you know: sampling, confidence intervals, and hypothesis testing applied to real A/B experiment data. Through interactive simulations, you'll design a valid A/B test, choose the right statistical test (t-test, chi-square), interpret p-values and effect sizes, and avoid common pitfalls like peeking and multiple comparisons. You'll run an actual A/B analysis in Python on a conversion-rate dataset — turning your marketing experiment experience into a data-scientist-grade skill.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Applied Statistics for Business Data", "Hypothesis Testing and A/B Experimentation"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Applied Statistics for Business Data", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Hypothesis Testing and A/B Experimentation", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 5",
            "title": "Capstone: Regression, Python Visualization, and Your First ML Model",
            "abstract": "Milestone session: combine everything into a portfolio-ready project. You'll build an end-to-end mini-project on a marketing spend dataset — retrieve and prepare data with Pandas, visualize relationships using Matplotlib and Seaborn (mapped from your Tableau mental model: charts, encodings, and dashboards), fit a linear regression with scikit-learn, and interpret coefficients as business recommendations. A brief, gentle intro to the scikit-learn workflow (train/test split, fit, predict) previews machine learning without overwhelming. Completing this project is a tangible step toward your junior data scientist goal — a portfolio artifact you can showcase in interviews.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Regression Analysis", "Data Visualization with Python (Matplotlib/Seaborn)", "Machine Learning Fundamentals (scikit-learn)"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Regression Analysis", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Data Visualization with Python (Matplotlib/Seaborn)", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Machine Learning Fundamentals (scikit-learn)", "level": "beginner"}
            ]
        }
    ]
}
